NAME
    freeze - pin a memory address by undoing writes to it

SYNOPSIS
    freeze add <space> <addr> [<value>]
    freeze list
    freeze remove <id>
    freeze clear

DESCRIPTION
    Pins hex address <addr> in writable memory space <space> to hex byte
    <value> (or to the byte currently stored there if <value> is omitted).
    Read-only memory spaces are refused.

    On cores with immediate write interception, any store of a different
    byte is undone immediately before subsequent instructions observe it,
    and 'freeze list' counts how many writes were blocked. On cores using
    the stable ABI, writes are checked at frame end and restored like a
    per-frame poke, and 'freeze list' counts frames whose end found the
    byte changed.

    Writes matching the pinned value are ignored and not counted, and the
    restore write itself does not re-trigger the freeze.

OPTIONS
    add <space> <addr> [<value>]
        Freeze <addr> in <space> at <value> (or its current byte).

    list
        List active freezes with their IDs, targets, values, and blocked
        counts.

    remove <id>
        Remove freeze #<id>.

    clear
        Remove all active freezes.

EXAMPLES
    freeze add WRAM 13c6
    freeze add WRAM 0dbf 63
    freeze list
    freeze remove 1
    freeze clear

EXIT STATUS
    0   Command completed (or usage/refusal message printed).
    1   No target attached, unknown space, invalid hex argument, or
        session service fault.

SEE ALSO
    cheat(1), watch(1), search(1), counters(1), spaces(1)
